			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source video for the target video edit, showing a girl holding a yellow plush rabbit toy against an indoor setting in two consecutive shots with a hand-held showcase style.\n<Picture 1> is the combined front-and-back reference image of the replacement pink plush rabbit, presented side by side on a plain white background.\n<Subject 1> is the pink plush rabbit whose front appearance (closed eyes with red stitched eyebrows, a small pink smile on a white muzzle, blushing pink cheeks, a small red bow tie at the neck, a cream belly patch with a small stitched \"x\", two long light-blue ribbon tears hanging down from the closed eyes, and long floppy ears with a yellow checkered inner lining along their length) comes from the left side of <Picture 1>, and whose back appearance (long pink plush ears from behind with the yellow checkered inner lining visible, plain pink back body, and a small white cotton tail at the lower back) comes from the right side of <Picture 1>.\n<Audio 1> is the original complete audio track of <Video 1>, including any ambient room tone, background music, and physical action sounds.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + reference generation + audio reuse] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. The yellow plush rabbit toy in both shots is replaced by a single pink plush rabbit character based on <Picture 1> (<Subject 1>), while the girl's outfit, hand positions, camera angles, indoor backgrounds, and overall showcase rhythm are preserved. <Audio 1> is reused unchanged as the target video's complete audio track.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (girl's outfit, hand positions, camera angles, indoor backgrounds, shot structure): partially_preserved - the girl's light-pink Hello Kitty-patterned loungewear, the wooden door decorations and Hello Kitty mat backgrounds, the camera framing, and the cut between the two shots are retained, but the yellow plush rabbit subject is replaced by <Subject 1> throughout.\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - the pink rabbit's face, ears, bow tie, belly patch, ribbon tears, fabric texture, and tail from <Picture 1> are retained.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - reused unchanged as the target video's complete audio track.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a warm, intimate hand-held showcase aesthetic with soft indoor lighting, matching <Video 1>.\n[Shot 1] A close-up to medium shot establishes a hand holding <Subject 1>, the pink plush rabbit referenced from <Picture 1>, at chest level against a white wooden door decorated with cartoon rabbit and bear cutouts and a small dangling figure. <Subject 1> has closed eyes with red stitched eyebrows, a small pink smile on a white muzzle, blushing pink cheeks, a small red bow tie at the neck, a cream belly patch with a small stitched \"x\", and two long light-blue ribbon tears hanging down from the closed eyes. The long floppy ears frame either side of the head, with a yellow checkered inner lining visible along their length. The hand adjusts its grip and presents the rabbit to the lens, with the girl's long dark hair visible on the right edge of the frame. The camera holds a near-static shot with a gentle natural sway from the hand.\n[Shot 2] At 00:06.500, the camera cuts to a slightly wider shot from a higher angle. The girl, wearing light-pink Hello Kitty-patterned loungewear, stands barefoot on a wooden floor with a Hello Kitty mat visible at the bottom of the frame and the decorated white door behind her. She holds <Subject 1> at waist level, presenting the full body of the pink plush rabbit. The cream belly patch, both feet, and the full length of the long ears with their yellow checkered inner lining are visible. The back view from the right side of <Picture 1> is referenced in the soft contour of the body, with a small white cotton tail implied at the lower back. The camera holds a near-static shot with gentle sway as the girl displays the rabbit.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe ambient room tone and physical action sounds from <Audio 1> continue throughout the target video, including the soft rustle of plush fabric as <Subject 1> is held and the gentle sound of the hand adjusting its grip.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nThe background music from <Audio 1> is reused unchanged as the complete audience-only score.\n"
